14. Transactions, Consistency & Availability
:BEGIN
CREATE (s:Student {id:'S010', name:'Neha'})
MATCH (c:Course {code:'BCA305'})
CREATE (s)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(c)
SET s.age = 19
:COMMIT

// Rollback example
:BEGIN
CREATE (s:Student {id:'S011', name:'Test'})
:ROLLBACK
Neo4j provides ACID transactions. All operations inside a transaction succeed or fail together → strong consistency. Availability is high with Causal Clustering (read replicas).
15. Complete Graph Application (Python + Neo4j)
from neo4j import GraphDatabase

driver = GraphDatabase.driver("bolt://localhost:7687", auth=("neo4j", "password"))

def create_student(tx, id, name):
    tx.run("CREATE (s:Student {id:$id, name:$name})", id=id, name=name)

def get_friends(tx, name):
    result = tx.run("""
        MATCH (p:Person {name:$name})-[:FRIENDS_WITH]-(f)
        RETURN f.name AS friend
    """, name=name)
    return [r["friend"] for r in result]

with driver.session() as session:
    session.execute_write(create_student, "S020", "Karan")
    friends = session.execute_read(get_friends, "Amit")
    print(friends)

driver.close()
CRUD + Relationship queries are natural in Neo4j.
Use cases: Social networks, recommendation engines, fraud detection, knowledge graphs.
